# RoadmapLearn

- Project: RoadmapLearn, a Django 6.1 monolith. Django templates + HTMX + Tailwind. No React, no separate SPA. SQLite for dev.
- Always read PROJECT_CONTEXT.md before starting a task, and keep it updated when models or rules change.
- Use existing model and field names exactly (Video, not Resource; quiz_pass_mark; User has xp, streak_days, last_active_date). Never rename without asking.
- Business logic lives in services.py with unit tests, not in views.
- Django 6 gotchas: format_html() needs at least one argument, so use mark_safe for static HTML. django-nested-admin is used for nested admin inlines.
- Never hardcode secrets. Secrets come from .env. Do not commit .env, db.sqlite3 or .venv.
- Ask before adding any new dependency.
- Work in small steps. After each task run the tests and `manage.py check`, then commit with a clear message. NEVER run `git push`; I push myself.
- If a model change or migration is needed, stop and tell me first.
- Always run Python as `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe`. Do not activate the venv, do not use conda or the global Python, and do not start `runserver`.
